==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|liggja|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*ligjaną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*legʰ-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈlɪcːa/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|ɪcːa|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|lá|lágu|legið}}

# to [[lie]] (on a bed etc.)
# to be [[located]], to [[lie]]
# to [[lead]] (e.g. of a road)

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj-s5|l|i|gg|j=j|mp=-}}

====Derived terms====
* [[allir vegir liggja til Rómar]]
* [[liggja fyrir]] (to [[lie]] in [[bed]])
* [[liggja í augum uppi]] (to be obvious)
* [[liggja í kör]]
* [[liggja í því]] (to be in trouble)
* [[liggja vel á]] (to be in hight spirits)
* [[liggja við]] (to be at stake)

